### Directives

- `docs/docs/directives/directives.mtf`

Contributor routing for compiler and build handoffs lives in
`docs/docs/directives/overview.mtf`. That file is not a public page import.
Template-specific directive meanings and comma-separated head items stay in
`docs/docs/templates/template-directives.mtf`. `docs/docs/directives/directives.mtf`
owns independent same-line source annotation stacking, unique directive names
and `$doc`/`$todo` declaration or statement attachment. Exact named `project` and
active-builder record fields plus the `$config` input contract stay in the
project-structure references. Root file roles are fixed at `@mod.moth`,
`@package.moth` and `@entry.moth`. A source annotation never selects an entry.
Capability-checked runtime title mutation remains deferred.

